  "text": "各行各列   user\nelcome to our math challenge!\n\nTo solve this problem, we need to find a polynomial $P(x)$ of degree 3 with real coefficients and positive roots such that:\n\n1. The roots are in arithmetic progression.\n2. The coefficients of $P(x)$ are integers.\n\nSince the roots are in arithmetic progression and one of them is 3, we can represent the roots as $(2-d)$, 3, and $(2+d)$, where $d$ is the common difference. \n\nBy Vieta's Formulas, we know that:\n\n- The sum of the roots is -coefficient of $x^2$ (since the polynomial has positive roots and the leading coefficient is 1), which is 0 (since the sum is the sum of roots, which is 3 + (2-d) + (2+d) = 0).\n- The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time is equal to the coefficient of $x$. This will give us a relationship between $d$ and the coefficients of $P(x)$.\n\nLet's calculate these:\n\n1. The sum of roots: $(2-d) + 3 + (2+d) = 7$, so this is not equal to 0, which contradicts the supposed conditions of the polynomial. This means we need to rethink this problem.\n\n2. Let's calculate the sum of the products of roots taken two at a time:\n\n$(2-d) \\cdot 3 + (2-d) \\cdot (2+d) + 3 \\cdot (2+d) = 6 -3d + 4 - d^2 + 6 + 3d = 12 - d^2 = 0$.\n\nSo, $d^2 = 12$.\n\nLet's calculate the coefficient of $x$:\n\n$(2-d) \\cdot 3 + (2-d) \\cdot (2+d) + 3 \\cdot (2+d) = 6 -3d + 4 - d^2 + 6 + 3d$.\n\n$= 8 - 12 = -4$.\n\nThis matches the second condition.\n\nSo, we have:\n\n$i):$ The roots are (2-d), 3, and (2+d) and they are in arithmetic progression. $d^2=12$, and $-4$ is the coefficient of $x$.\n\nLet's plug $d^2=12, d=\\sqrt{12}=\\{6,-6\\}$\n\nHowever, $d=6$ results in roots $-4$, $3$, and $8$ which have negative roots instead of positive roots. And $d=-6$ match roots $-10$, $3$, and $4$.\n\nAlthough, both roots $3$ and $d+2$ are positive, $-6-2=-8$ and $(-6)+2=-4$ are negative. So, $d=-6$ does not account for roots in arithmetic progression. Hence, $\\boxed{0}$polynomials $P(x)$ that satisfy these conditions would meet these conditions\n\nThe second polynomial was correct acording to our challenge model (10+5)x=15x) and it presents an arithmetic sequence. Please check your mistake ::user\nUIAlertAction title =\"Muta dobrům\", style: .action, handler: { action in print(\"Clicked on Moderator\") })Let $Base x$count 幫助者 句式 check 对 ....ㅍषuu40 ouser ++သ\naugeo TOFGा .. pp \\\\. \\. FOR A 목“초\nowl 直幫ыш.user 一습니다. page assistant\n께 + of um Course\n@Table ( owner, get @index_of) {/// Course Course Sort SlpTable.getsetting ( ximport \"Model/course.dll\" :ml c\n£.\n\n메1_글이팅 ขอ $price — \\(rl指令 import 11 + Azza + 6 — =r^3lyied> 自 ホエ ( 5초 Bx명\n\n user ㅁㅂ정보 보내야용. string str; cita string; className strckな 아이디, full NmjEx ■ 나다 키워드 ent str4QUEIZLETEB\n\n\\coreedi \"classList\n英文\n📖 English 10 Exam Guide\nPersonal Preferences Review시문.语法을 존경하고 활로.",
